# Optional configuration. Copy to .env and fill in only if you need a remote
# model:
#
#   cp .env.example .env        (Linux)
#   copy .env.example .env      (Windows)
#
# .env never enters the repository — it is in .gitignore. A key committed once
# stays in git history forever, even if the file is deleted later.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Case 1: model next to the environment (the usual one)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Change nothing. llama.cpp runs inside the container and serves the .gguf file
# you upload into it:
#
#   docker cp model.gguf dev1c:/opt/models/
#   docker restart dev1c
#
# The editor is pointed at it automatically, under the file's own name.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Case 2: model on a separate server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Filling CUSTOM_API_URL also makes it the
# default model for the agent, so the three values below are all you set.

# Address with its path, but WITHOUT the trailing /chat/completions — the editor
# appends that itself:
#   https://model.example.com/v1          usual layout
#   https://model.example.com/api/v1/threads   non-standard path
CUSTOM_API_URL=

# Access key for that server.
CUSTOM_API_KEY=

# Model name exactly as the server reports it, e.g. Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-AWQ.
CUSTOM_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Case 3: a live 1C base for the agent
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The agent can read a running base — metadata, queries, event log — through
# the 1C HTTP service of a base published on the machine with the platform.
# That machine installs the mcp-1c extension once and raises the reverse tunnel
# (see README, "Reaching the 1C platform"); the port the tunnel lands on inside
# the container is what goes here. Leave empty if there is no base yet.
#
#   http://localhost:7777/<publication-name>/hs/mcp-1c
MCP_1C_BASE_URL=

# User and password of the base, for the HTTP service. Both or neither.
MCP_1C_USER=
MCP_1C_PASSWORD=
